laurel 2301: battery gauge + charger on the PMI632 over SPMI (new bsd/dev/laurel_pmi632.c). SweetBattery: the topaz SM5602/bq2589x I2C path (chips the Mi A3 does not have) and the dead PM6150 reader are replaced by laurel_pmi632_sample(): QG voltage/current, ADC5 battery NTC (100k table), SoC from the saved SDAM value or the QG PON OCV (Sunwoda 25 C OCV table) + coulomb count + rest-OCV drift fix + "terminated" = 100 %, saved to our SDAM record once a minute; SMB5 input limit from APSD/Type-C Rp (HW_AUTO again on unplug or without a limit), software JEITA zones for FCC/FV (Mi A3 DT values) with the warm-zone input suspend above FV + 50 mV, every write read back. Charger control only with a working battery NTC and the hardware JEITA hard limits at the Linux 0/60 C codes (written when not); no good NTC sample for 30 s = 500 mA at 4100 mV and control off; boot FCC/FV written back when control turns off on a write failure; FCC <= 500 mA at unplug. Review fixes 2026-11-01 (B1, M1-M4, m4, m5). Safety re-check fixes: the NTC watchdog runs before any early return of the sample and from its own 10 s thread_call (independent of SweetBattery); every control-off writes 500 mA / 4100 mV first (boot limits only when not above that), also when control cannot turn on with SMB5 ours; a USB input suspend of an earlier boot is released at start; hard-limit accept window only on the safe side. Unattended-safety follow-up: a failed safe write is retried every 10 s by the guard timer until it reads back (the timer never stops while one is pending); FV is written even when its read fails; the write-check failure and every battery self-check failure (QG type, no battery, vbat) also write the safe limits and release a left input suspend when SMB5 is EE 0 (laurelbatt=0 / laurelchg=0: no writes); before a system sleep (IOPMrootDomain will-sleep) the charger gets 500 mA / 4100 mV. Publishes the negroni 0271/0365 key set (CurrentCapacity, IsCharging, FullyCharged, ExternalConnected, AdapterDetails with FamilyCode, Voltage, Amperage, InstantAmperage, Temperature, CycleCount, times to full/empty). Self-check lines: 'LAUREL BATTERY: on: PMI632 QG soc N% ...' / 'off: <reason>', 'LAUREL CHARGER: on: ...' / 'off: <reason>'. Kill switches laurelbatt=0, laurelchg=0 (sweetbattery=0 still gives the static fallback).

