+/*
+ * laurel 2301 (Xiaomi Mi A3, SM6125 + PMI632): battery gauge and charger over SPMI.
+ *
+ * The Mi A3 has no SM5602 / bq2589x I2C chips (topaz 0091/0148): the gauge (QG) and the charger
+ * (SMB5) are blocks of the PMI632 at SPMI SID 2 (pmi632.dtsi, laurel_sprout-trinket-battery.dtsi).
+ *   QG     0x4800  type 0x0d; LAST_ADC_V 0xc0 (194.637 uV/LSB), LAST_BURST_AVG_I 0xc6 (152.588 uA/LSB
+ *                  on the 5 A subtype 3, 305.176 on subtype 4; + = discharge), S7 PON OCV 0x70
+ *                  (qg-reg.h, qg-defs.h V_RAW_TO_UV / I_RAW_TO_UA, qg-util.c)
+ *   SDAM   0xb100  Linux QG record: valid 0x46, soc 0x47, learned capacity 0x68 (mAh), cycle buckets
+ *                  0x58 (8 x u16); our own record 0xa8..0xaf (after the Linux area, 0x45..0xa3)
+ *   VADC   0x3100  ADC5 user channel: BAT_THERM_PU2 (0x4a), ratiometric, 100k NTC table of
+ *                  qcom-vadc-common.c adcmap_batt_therm_100k (lut index 0), full scale 0x70e4
+ *   SMB5   CHGR 0x1000, DCDC 0x1100, BATIF 0x1200, USBIN 0x1300, TYPEC 0x1500 (smb5-reg.h; PMI632
+ *          params of qpnp-smb5.c: FCC 50 mA steps max 3000, FV 3600 + 10 mV steps, ICL 50 mA steps)
+ * Battery: Sunwoda/Feimaotui 4030-4040 mAh, 4.40 V (batterydata-wingtech-*-4v4-4040mah.dtsi); the OCV
+ * table below is the 25 C column of the Sunwoda pc-temp-v1-lut.
+ *
+ * SoC. The Linux QG computes the SoC in software (qg-soc.c with the battery profile). Here:
+ *   start  saved SoC (our SDAM record, else the Linux QG SDAM SoC) after a warm reset; after a cold
+ *          start the saved SoC only when it is within 10 % of the SoC of the PON OCV (QG S7, measured
+ *          before the load), else the PON OCV SoC; no OCV: the saved SoC, else the voltage curve.
+ *   run    coulomb count of the QG burst current over the learned capacity (SDAM, else 4000 mAh), in
+ *          uAh (the master value; only a clamp or a correction writes it back); at rest (|I| < 30 mA
+ *          for 30 s, on battery) a drift of more than 5 % to the OCV SoC is corrected by 1 % per
+ *          sample; charger "terminated" at FV 4400 mV with a charger in = 100 % (held while plugged);
+ *          below 3300 mV for 30 s on battery = 0 % (critical), else never below 1 %.
+ *   save   our SDAM record once a minute when the SoC changed (owner check: EE 0). [I] 0xa8..0xaf
+ *          are past the Linux QG area (0x45..0xa3) and below the PBS PON OCV (0xbc); not proven free.
+ * Charger (HLOS owns SMB5 on this device: Android 4.14 qpnp-smb5 writes it). On only with a working
+ * battery NTC and the hardware JEITA hard limits at the Linux values (0 C / 60 C, written when not).
+ * The boot FCC/FV are saved. With a charger in:
+ *   input  APSD result: DCP / QC 2000 mA, float 1000 mA, CDP 1500 mA, SDP: the Type-C Rp current
+ *          (3.0 A -> 2000, 1.5 A -> 1500), else the hardware's (HW_AUTO); SW_OVERRIDE_HC mode of
+ *          smb5-lib.c smblib_icl_override (USBIN_MODE_CHG, no ICL override, override after APSD).
+ *          Unplug: HW_AUTO again, input un-suspended, FCC at most 500 mA until the next step.
+ *   JEITA  software zones on the NTC (negroni 0277 rule, Mi A3 DT values: COLD 0 C / HOT 60 C hard
+ *          limits stay in the hardware, FV 4100 mV above 44 C): < 0 C 0, 0..10 C 400 mA, 10..15 C
+ *          1200 mA, 15..44 C 3000 mA, 44..58 C 1500 mA at 4100 mV, >= 58 C 0. A zone with more current
+ *          only 1.5 C inside it. FCC 0 = no charge. Warm zone with VBAT > FV + 50 mV: USB input
+ *          suspended until VBAT < FV - 50 mV (step-chg-jeita.c handle_jeita).
+ *   NTC    no good NTC sample for 30 s: 500 mA at 4100 mV, control off (never a stale temperature).
+ *          The watchdog runs first in every sample (before any gauge read can return early) and from
+ *          its own 10 s thread_call, so it does not depend on the SweetBattery poll.
+ *   off    every control-off writes 500 mA / 4100 mV first; the boot limits only when not above that.
+ *          Control cannot turn on (no NTC, write check, hard limits, no timer) or the battery self-check
+ *          fails, with SMB5 ours: 500 mA / 4100 mV too. A safe write that fails is retried every 10 s by
+ *          the guard timer until it reads back (the timer never stops while one is pending). Before a
+ *          system sleep: 500 mA / 4100 mV (the timer does not run while asleep). laurelbatt=0 /
+ *          laurelchg=0 are kill switches: no writes, the previous limits stay.
+ *          A USB input suspend left by an earlier boot is released at start (also with control off),
+ *          ours before a power off / restart (lock-free USBIN lane).
+ *   Every write is read back; a failed write turns the charger control off (the reads stay).
+ * SMB1355 (parallel charger on QUP0 SE1 I2C) is not used: the PMI632 charges alone (max 3 A FCC).
+ *
+ * Self-check (laurel_pmi632_init): QG type 0x0d, battery present, a sane voltage; else
+ * "LAUREL BATTERY: off: <reason>" and SweetBattery keeps its static fallback. Charger control needs
+ * the NTC, the SMB5 CHGR/USBIN APIDs owned by EE 0 and the hard limits ("LAUREL CHARGER: off: ..."
+ * otherwise, reads stay).
+ * Kill switches: laurelbatt=0 (no PMI632 reads at all), laurelchg=0 (no charger writes).
+ */
